---
import Picture from './Picture.astro';
const { images } = Astro.props;
const streaks = [images[1], images[2], images[0], images[3]];
const metrics = [
  ['Feature adoption rate', 'The percentage of active users who start a streak in a given week.'],
  ['Streak retention rate', 'The percentage of users who maintain an active streak week over week, with checkpoints at 7, 14, and 30 days.'],
  ['Days active per user', 'The average number of days per week a user posts or completes a qualifying action to maintain their streak.'],
  ['Share rate', 'The percentage of users with a streak who successfully share it to their social channels.'],
];
---
<dl class="meta-row"><div><dt>Discipline</dt><dd>Mobile app UI design</dd></div><div><dt>Duration</dt><dd>6 months</dd></div><div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Cooking streaks · Cooking challenges</dd></div><div><dt>Organization</dt><dd>Pepper</dd></div></dl>

<section class="project-context">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Cooking streaks</p><h2>A little progress.<br/><em>A lasting habit.</em></h2></div>
  <div><p>The Cooking Streak feature turns engagement into a clear, game-like goal. A prominent counter and flames make progress visible, while a five-week milestone, gift box, and “CLAIM” button make the reward easy to understand.</p><p>Streaks appear on the user’s profile to recognize their engagement and in a pop-up after posting to encourage them to keep going. The proposed Instagram “Share Streak” call to action adds social proof and gives users a way to celebrate their consistency.</p></div>
</section>

<div class="pepper-screens pepper-streaks" aria-label="Cooking streak interface designs">
  {streaks.map((im, i) => <figure><button class="zoom-button" data-zoom data-caption={im.alt} aria-label={`Enlarge ${im.alt.toLowerCase()}`}><Picture image={im} alt={im.alt} eager={i===0} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 85vw, (max-width: 1000px) 43vw, 23vw"/><span class="zoom-label" aria-hidden="true">View detail ↗</span></button></figure>)}
</div>

<section class="project-context pepper-section">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">The rhythm</p><h2>Start cooking.<br/><em>Keep coming back.</em></h2></div>
  <div class="pepper-rules"><div><h3>Start a streak</h3><p>Post a recipe on the app.</p></div><div><h3>Keep it alive</h3><p>Post at least once every seven days. The weekly window makes consistency achievable without requiring a post every single day.</p></div></div>
</section>

<section class="pepper-section" aria-labelledby="pepper-metrics">
  <p class="eyebrow">Key KPIs &amp; metrics</p><h2 id="pepper-metrics">What Was Measured</h2>
  <p class="pepper-note">Success measures for evaluating the feature.</p>
  <dl class="pepper-metrics">{metrics.map(([name, description]) => <div><dt>{name}</dt><dd>{description}</dd></div>)}</dl>
</section>

<section class="pepper-section" aria-labelledby="pepper-challenges">
  <div class="project-context pepper-challenge-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Cooking challenges</p><h2 id="pepper-challenges">An invitation<br/><em>to join in.</em></h2></div><div><p>A challenge invitation introduces the opportunity to earn extra Spice and be featured on Pepper Global. The challenge feed brings the host, featured dish, participation count, and entry action into one view.</p></div></div>
  <div class="pepper-screens pepper-challenges" aria-label="Cooking challenge interface designs">
    {images.slice(4).map(im => <figure><button class="zoom-button" data-zoom data-caption={im.alt} aria-label={`Enlarge ${im.alt.toLowerCase()}`}><Picture image={im} alt={im.alt} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 85vw, 38vw"/><span class="zoom-label" aria-hidden="true">View detail ↗</span></button></figure>)}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pepper-section" aria-labelledby="pepper-trivia">
  <div class="project-context pepper-challenge-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Interactive feature demo</p><h2 id="pepper-trivia">Try the<br/><em>daily trivia.</em></h2></div><div><p>A playable look at the daily food trivia feature I helped bring into testing. Tap “YES CHEF!” to explore the demo.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://java-ahead-12527439.figma.site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo in a new tab ↗</a></div></div>
  <div class="pepper-trivia-frame"><span class="phone-button phone-button-action" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="phone-button phone-button-volume" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="phone-button phone-button-volume-down" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="phone-button phone-button-camera" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="phone-button phone-button-power" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="pepper-phone-screen"><div class="phone-top" aria-hidden="true"><span class="phone-island"></span></div><iframe src="https://java-ahead-12527439.figma.site/" title="Pepper daily food trivia interactive demo" loading="lazy" allow="fullscreen" allowfullscreen></iframe><div class="phone-bottom" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div></div>
  <div class="pepper-trivia-result"><h3>13% increase in D7 retention</h3><p>Among 3,000 active users who entered the trivia beta, day-seven app retention was 13% higher than in a control group of 3,000 users without the feature over the same period.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="project-context pepper-section">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Design considerations</p><h2>Consistency<br/><em>with breathing room.</em></h2></div>
  <div><h3>Habit formation &amp; retention</h3><p>A forgiving weekly window could support longer-term retention without punishing users for missing a single day.</p><h3>Depth vs. breadth of engagement</h3><p>The definition of a qualifying action matters. Letting low-effort interactions sustain a streak could encourage surface-level activity instead of actual cooking and recipe uploads. The goal is to support meaningful participation, not just preserve a counter.</p></div>
</section>

<style>
  .pepper-screens{display:grid;gap:24px;align-items:start;margin:48px 0 72px}
  .pepper-streaks{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}
  .pepper-screens figure{margin:0;min-width:0}
  .pepper-screens .zoom-button{display:block;width:100%;border:1px solid var(--line);background:white;padding:0}
  .pepper-streaks figure:last-child .zoom-button{overflow:hidden}
  .pepper-streaks figure:last-child :global(img){transform:scale(1.012);transform-origin:center}
  .pepper-section{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:56px;margin-top:64px}
  .pepper-section>.eyebrow{margin-bottom:18px}
  .pepper-note{color:var(--muted);margin-top:20px}
  .pepper-rules{display:grid;gap:28px}
  .pepper-section h3{margin-bottom:12px}
  .pepper-section p+h3{margin-top:30px}
  .pepper-metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px 64px;margin:36px 0 0}
  .pepper-metrics div{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:20px}
  .pepper-metrics dt{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px}
  .pepper-metrics dd{color:var(--muted);margin:0;max-width:55ch}
  .pepper-challenges{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));max-width:820px;margin-inline:auto;gap:40px}
  .pepper-challenge-intro{margin-top:0}
  .pepper-trivia-result{max-width:620px;margin:0 auto 64px;text-align:center}
  .pepper-trivia-result h3{margin-bottom:12px}
  .pepper-trivia-result p{color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65}
  .pepper-trivia-frame{position:relative;width:calc(100% - 12px);max-width:414px;margin:48px auto 72px;padding:8px;background:linear-gradient(110deg,#505154,#18191b 12%,#202123 85%,#555659);border:1px solid #5a5b5e;border-radius:54px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px #17181a,inset 0 0 0 4px #38393c,0 24px 48px -20px rgba(10,18,30,.35),0 5px 12px rgba(10,18,30,.12)}
  .pepper-phone-screen{overflow:hidden;border:2px solid #050506;border-radius:44px;background:#fff}
  .phone-top{height:38px;position:relative;background:#fff}
  .phone-island{position:absolute;width:108px;height:30px;left:50%;top:6px;transform:translateX(-50%);border-radius:20px;background:#08090b;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #17181b}
  .phone-island::after{content:"";position:absolute;right:10px;top:8px;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle at 38% 35%,#24354c,#101724 45%,#020306 70%);box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #0e0f12}
  .phone-bottom{height:24px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#fff}
  .phone-bottom span{width:110px;height:4px;background:#08090b;border-radius:4px}
  .phone-button{position:absolute;width:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#18191b,#66676a,#242527);border-radius:2px;pointer-events:none}
  .phone-button-action{left:-3px;top:100px;height:24px}
  .phone-button-volume{left:-3px;top:147px;height:42px}
  .phone-button-volume-down{left:-3px;top:204px;height:42px}
  .phone-button-camera{right:-3px;bottom:165px;height:48px}
  .phone-button-power{right:-3px;top:167px;height:76px}
  .pepper-trivia-frame iframe{display:block;width:100%;height:780px;border:0;background:#fff;clip-path:inset(2px round 36px)}
  @media(max-width:1000px){.pepper-streaks{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));max-width:760px;margin-inline:auto}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.pepper-screens{grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:390px;gap:32px}.pepper-metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.pepper-section{padding-top:36px;margin-top:44px}}
</style>
